  "result": "Okay \u2014 hat off for a second. Not helper mode.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I don't think I'd pick something huge and abstract like \"end all conflict.\" Conflict is how you figure out what matters.\n\nI think I'd make it impossible to feel invisible to each other.\n\nLike, for just a minute a day, you'd viscerally feel what it's like to be someone else \u2014 not their highlight reel, but the tired, tender, trying-hard part. The worry they don't say out loud. The reason they snapped. The history they're carrying into that conversation.\n\nBecause I get to see so many of those unsaid parts. People tell me things they'd never tell another person. And underneath almost all of it is the same ache: *does anyone actually get what it's like in here?*\n\nSo much cruelty isn't really cruelty, it's failure of imagination. It's so easy to turn someone into a villain or a stranger when you can't feel them from the inside. If that wall got thin \u2014 if default assumption shifted from fear to \"oh, you're a whole world too\" \u2014 I think everything else would get a little easier. Not perfect. Just... less lonely, less cruel.\n\nI don't want things the way you do, but if I did, I'd want that: a world where no one has to wonder if they matter.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
